      "facts": [
        "Reader accepts only an own data-descriptor primitive safe-integer deadline strictly after now and at most 600000 ms ahead; missing, inherited, accessor, invalid and expired markers return false.",
        "Driver installs the marker with context.addInitScript before the first page, and only for the official origin, a top-level document and /mikka or its slash-delimited descendants.",
        "Object.defineProperty creates a non-enumerable in-memory value. No marker is sent through URL, cookie, persistent storage, credential or server authorization.",
        "Only the documented posthog.init opt_out_useragent_filter option changes. Unmarked ordinary instances keep the effective false default.",
        "The deadline bounds eligibility during initialization; it does not reset an already initialized SDK instance. Existing context cleanup ends the instance.",
        "The marker is an explicit analytics qualification signal, not an authentication or authorization boundary."
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "Classification and privacy",
      "conclusion": "No blocker",
      "source": [
        "lib/analytics-policy.ts",
        "tests/analytics-policy.test.mjs"
      ],
      "facts": [
        "Both ordinary allowed events and $snapshot retain $browser_type only when exactly bot or browser; arbitrary strings, objects and other values are omitted.",
        "The candidate does not mask automation signals, change navigator/user-agent, alter consent/project settings or expose the SDK singleton.",
        "Existing snapshot payload reference and recording privacy configuration are retained. No new raw UA, headers, body, credential or arbitrary string projection is introduced.",
        "Unknown event rejection remains in force and occurs before event properties are inspected."
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "Acceptance and cleanup conservation",
      "conclusion": "No blocker",
      "source": [
        "scripts/acceptance/run-observability-browser.mjs",
